# The GT bridge is edited on the Windows machine that has Subiekt GT installed
# and copied into this repository verbatim. Git must therefore not rewrite its
# bytes on the way in or out: with normalisation on, every sync from that
# machine produces a whole-file diff in line endings alone, which buries the
# real change and makes review useless.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion only. Textual diff and blame are
# unaffected.
#
# Note the deliberate divergence from the repository's `.editorconfig`, which
# asks for CRLF: that file describes what an editor should WRITE, and the
# editor writing these files is on the other machine. The sibling nexo bridge
# under `bridge/` is edited here and keeps the repository default.
* -text
